# Fixed 2026-09-30, defect 131's class, lane recovery-b2 (lane recovery-b1's
# report, U1), beside `fixedbugs-130-a-declaration-past-a-bracket-never-closed`.
# Symptom: a declaration in braces, `record P {` over its fields with no `}`,
# cost the lexer's `unclosed_bracket` and the habit's own message at one
# token, and its braces read the rest of the file as members, so `record P {`
# over `x: i64` above `function main()` cost four messages for one mistake
# and the declarations below it were never read. Cause: the braces' `}` was
# sought by counting braces to the file's end, past where the lexer named
# the `{` never closed, and the two reports at the `{` were both said. Now
# the braces end where the lexer named them (`brace_habit.closer`), and at a
# `{` the parser speaks at, which the language writes only for a map, the
# habit's message is the one said (`parse/unclosed.withdrawn`); the lines
# after it are read as the declarations they are. No fix.

